## 11. Strategy Baseline Compare

### 11.1 This Is For
- Put `P1` / `P1+BL` / `P1-LiveFull` / current search candidate into one reproducible Node-side comparison.
- Keep baseline replay and candidate search separated, then merge them into one report for final judgment.

### 11.2 Command
```bash
node scripts/compare_strategy_baselines.js
```

### 11.3 How To Run
- Run from repo root.
- Default baseline view is `riskParity / balanced`.
- Optional overrides:
  - `WF_BASELINE_ALLOCATION_STYLE`
  - `WF_BASELINE_RISK_PREF`
- The script automatically reads the latest `strategy_search_*.manifest.json` and uses the top candidate.
- If no `strategy_search_*.manifest.json` exists yet, it will clearly warn and fall back to the default candidate config.

### 11.4 Result Files
- `test result/strategy_baseline_compare_YYYY-MM-DD.json`
- `test result/strategy_baseline_compare_YYYY-MM-DD.md`
- `test result/strategy_baseline_compare_YYYY-MM-DD.csv`

### 11.5 Current Output
